<h2>My Background</h2>
	<p>
		I&apos;ve spent over 12 years working in enterprise software, specializing in backend systems and large-scale insurance platforms. 
		My current role involves building, maintaining, and improving mission-critical applications. 
		Over time, I&apos;ve developed a passion for simplifying complex systems, automating manual processes, and mentoring new developers.
		But I&apos;ve never been content with just maintaining what exists. 
		I&apos;m driven to learn, explore, and create—and that&apos;s what this blog is all about.
	</p>
<h2>Life Long Learning</h2>
	<p>
		I&apos;m currently pursuing my Master&apos;s in Computer Science, with a focus on machine learning and artificial intelligence. 
		I split my time between real-world projects, academic work, and raising a family (and the occasional World Of Warcraft).
		You&apos;ll often find me working through learning models late at night, debugging deployment pipelines, or writing blog posts when I'm not engaged in family events and activities.
	</p>

	<h2>My Goals</h2>
	<p>
		MakingCode.io is my platform to document and share the next phase of my journey as a software engineer and graduate student.Through this blog, I aim to:
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>Solidify my understanding of machine learning, AI, and cloud architecture by teaching what I learn.</li>
			<li>Document my learning process and projects.</li>
			<li>Provide insights into real-world applications of AI and cloud technologies.</li>
			<li>Build real-world experience building ML-powered projects deployed using modern tools like FastAPI, Vue.js, and cloud platforms such as AWS.</li>
